{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/cww9lo","slide":6,"text":"ICA matters because annotators found it visually informative, not because component identities are anatomical. The next analysis should test whether frozen ICA-derived measures add predictive or explanatory value after Local Norm features. If they merely reproduce a simple signed difference, the simpler comparator wins.\n\n[Sources]\n/home/jibby2k1/Documents/ChatGPT/Neuromechanics/NeuRev-Workbench-unsupervised-ica-eval/Outputs/NeuronIdentifiability/spon_ca_burst_identifiability_paper_v1_v8/03_trace_atlas/trace_metrics.tsv\n/home/jibby2k1/Documents/ChatGPT/Neuromechanics/NeuRev-Workbench-unsupervised-ica-eval/Outputs/NeuronIdentifiability/spon_ca_burst_identifiability_paper_v1_v8/09_ica_statistical_test_suite/summary.json\n/home/jibby2k1/Documents/ChatGPT/Neuromechanics/NeuRev-Workbench-unsupervised-ica-eval/Outputs/NeuronIdentifiability/spon_ca_burst_identifiability_paper_v1_v8/10_representation_confirmation/summary.json\n[/Sources]"}